# Original ROM — provide your own local copy (sha1 in checksum.sha1)
/baserom.gba

# Build outputs
*.gba
*.elf
*.map
*.o
*.obj
*.d
.dep/
.deps/

# Shiftability harness outputs (scripts/shiftcheck/ -- make shiftcheck): the shifted
# -build scratch dir + the ld response file. (fireemblem8_relocs.elf/.map are *.elf/*.map.)
build/shiftcheck/
/objects.lst

# Asset build intermediates (Phase 0). The COMMITTED source is the editable
# PNG / JASC .pal under graphics/; these are REGENERATED from it by the Makefile's
# gbagfx rules (%.4bpp: %.png, %.lz: %, %.gbapal: %.pal, ...) and must never be
# committed. baserom.gba is not in their build chain.
*.1bpp
*.4bpp
*.8bpp
*.gbapal
*.lz
*.rl
*.fk
*.4bpp.h

# TSA battle-background intermediates (D309). The editable source is the .png;
# FETSATOOL regenerates these byte-for-byte (mirrors ../fireemblem8u which also
# gitignores *.feimg*.bin / *.fetsa*.bin). The 7 btl_bg below are a plain linear
# 4bpp tile-strip in the ROM (not a TSA screen-image): their fe8u .png rebuilds
# the .feimg3.bin tiles byte-for-byte via gbagfx (wave-2, axis #6), so the
# .feimg3.bin is now a generated artifact (.png is the committed editable
# source). Only the paired .fetsa3.bin tilemap -- which has no editable fe8u
# source -- stays COMMITTED (re-included below; FLOOR, mirrors fe8u's .map.bin).
*.feimg*.bin
*.fetsa*.bin
!graphics/btl_bg/btl_bg_14.fetsa3.bin
!graphics/btl_bg/btl_bg_27.fetsa3.bin
!graphics/btl_bg/btl_bg_33.fetsa3.bin
!graphics/btl_bg/btl_bg_55.fetsa3.bin
!graphics/btl_bg/btl_bg_58.fetsa3.bin
!graphics/btl_bg/btl_bg_59.fetsa3.bin
!graphics/btl_bg/btl_bg_60.fetsa3.bin

# Statscreen TSAs (wave-6, axis #6). The COMMITTED editable source is the .tmap
# tilemap (fireemblem8u graphics/statscreen/*.tmap); scripts/tmap2tsa.py
# regenerates these .bin byte-for-byte (per-file --width/--height in the Makefile
# rule), and the generic %.lz rule then produces the committed-into-ROM .bin.lz.
# The .bin is a build artifact and must never be committed. (Tsa_Statscreen-
# EquipedWeaponHighlight.bin stays committed -- 2 trailing pad bytes the standard
# tmap2tsa output omits, so it has no byte-exact .tmap source.)
graphics/gmapunit/Tsa_StatscreenBG.bin
graphics/gmapunit/Tsa_StatscreenHalo.bin
graphics/gmapunit/Tsa_StatscreenEquipmentBG.bin

# OpAnim / IntelligentSystems TSAs (wave-6, axis #6). The COMMITTED editable source
# is the .png (graphics/opanim/OpAnim*.png + graphics/misc_gfx{,3}/{OpAnim*,
# IntelligentSystems}.png); FETSATOOL regenerates these Tsa_*.bin byte-for-byte
# (per-asset flags in the Makefile rule), and the generic %.lz rule produces the
# committed-into-ROM .bin.lz. The Tsa_*.bin is a build artifact, never committed.
graphics/misc_gfx/Tsa_OpAnimEirika.bin
graphics/misc_gfx/Tsa_OpAnimEirikaBlur1.bin
graphics/misc_gfx/Tsa_OpAnimEirikaBlur2.bin
graphics/misc_gfx/Tsa_OpAnimEirikaBlur3.bin
graphics/misc_gfx/Tsa_OpAnimEphraim.bin
graphics/misc_gfx/Tsa_OpAnimEphraimBlur1.bin
graphics/misc_gfx/Tsa_OpAnimGenericCharacterBG.bin
graphics/misc_gfx/Tsa_OpAnimWorldMap.bin
graphics/misc_gfx/Tsa_OpAnimWorldMapFog.bin
graphics/misc_gfx3/Tsa_IntelligentSystems.bin

# Battle-animation compressing-linker intermediates (BA1). The COMMITTED editable
# sources are banim/*_motion.s (OAM/script/modes macros) + graphics/banim/*.png +
# graphics/banim/*.agbpal. The motion .s is assembled to banim/*_motion.o and its
# sections objcopy-extracted to banim/*_oam_l.bin / *_oam_r.bin / *_modes.bin, then
# LZ-compressed and folded by scripts/arm_compressing_linker.py into the single
# banim/data_banim.o (+ .sym.o). All of these are build artifacts (the .o/.lz are
# already covered above); the extracted .bin must never be committed. mirrors
# ../fireemblem8u's `banim/*.bin` ignore. baserom.gba is not in this build chain.
banim/*.bin

# Sound build intermediates (Phase 1 Music). The COMMITTED source is the editable
# AIFF (.aif) under sound/direct_sound_samples/; the raw GBA PCM blob (.bin) is
# REGENERATED from it by `sound/%.bin: sound/%.aif` (tools/aif2pcm) and must never
# be committed. baserom.gba is not in this build chain. (Scoped to sound/ so the
# graphics/map *.bin -- the editable-source ones are ignored separately below, the
# 7 ObjectType blobs stay committed -- are unaffected.)
sound/**/*.bin

# Chapter map + tileset-config tilemaps (D309). The COMMITTED editable sources are
# graphics/map/layout/<name>.mar + .json (63 chapter maps, built by MARTOMAP) and
# graphics/map/<name>.S + tile_config.inc + terrains.inc (11 tile configs, built by
# as+objcopy). The flat .bin they produce is a build artifact and must never be
# committed (mirrors ../fireemblem8u's graphics/map/layout/*.bin +
# graphics/map/*TileConfiguration*.bin ignores, adapted to JP's flat .bin layout).
# Every *Map*.bin has a .mar source; the 7 *ObjectType*.bin are LZ'd gfx with no
# editable source and STAY committed (not matched by these globs). The .bin.lz is
# already covered by the *.lz rule above.
graphics/map/*Map*.bin
graphics/map/*TileConfiguration*.bin

# Compiler-generated assembly (agbcc emits src/x.s next to src/x.c).
# Hand-written assembly lives in asm/ and is tracked.
src/*.s
# ...except hand-written real-source assembly TUs (like fe8u's src/*.s): the BIOS
# syscall wrappers. These are COMMITTED sources, not generated, and count as matching-C.
!src/libagbsyscall.s
!src/call_via.s
!src/agbsyscall_80D5244.s
!src/m4a_1.s
!src/arm.s
!src/arm_call.s
!src/j_ClearOam.s
!src/nullsub_111.s
!src/nullsub_3.s
src/data/*.s
src/data/map/*.s
src/data/**/*.s
# ...except hand-written AP (sprite/object animation) definition sources: these
# replace the opaque INCBIN-of-.bin wrappers with editable include/ap.inc macro
# .s source (axis #6). They are COMMITTED sources (no .c twin generates them).
!src/data/anim_arrow_trap/dat_anim_arrow_trap.s
!src/data/anim_fire_trap/dat_anim_fire_trap.s
!src/data/anim_pike_trap/dat_anim_pike_trap.s
!src/data/anim_trap_gas/dat_anim_trap_gas.s
!src/data/anim_player_rank_fog/dat_anim_player_rank_fog.s
!src/data/anim_worldmap_skirmish/dat_anim_worldmap_skirmish.s
!src/data/anim_mapanim_statgain/dat_anim_mapanim_statgain.s
!src/data/anim_mapanim_berserk_silence/dat_anim_mapanim_berserk_silence.s
!src/data/anim_mapanim_torch/dat_anim_mapanim_torch.s
!src/data/anim_mapanim_torchfx/dat_anim_mapanim_torchfx.s
!src/data/anim_mapanim_objects/dat_anim_mapanim_objects.s
# ...and the unit-icon move (AP) motion tables: editable fe8u .2byte-offset .s
# source replacing the opaque data_<ADDR>.bin INCBIN wrappers (axis #6, wave4).
!src/data/unit_icon_move_motion/*.s
# ...and the worldmap nation-highlight (AP) motion tables (region-different from
# fe8u src/data/worldmap/anim_worldmap_highlight.s): editable .2byte-offset .s
# source replacing the Ap_WmHightLightMap*.bin INCBIN wrappers (axis #6, wave7).
!src/data/Ap_WmHightLightMap3_ref/*.s
!src/data/Ap_WmHightLightMap6_ref/*.s
# ...and the prep-screen funds-banner AP-motion table (AP_DrawPreparationsBanner,
# JP-only) interleaved with Img_PrepFunds.4bpp.lz, like fe8u's interleaved AP .s.
!src/data/worldmap_gmapunit/dat_worldmap_gmapunit_p1601.s
# ...and the warp/prep unit-swap cursor AP-motion table (gUnkData_2 / g085A0EA0):
# region-same with fe8u src/data/ui/anim_085A0EA0.s, replaces the 11 split
# g085A0EA0_*.bin INCBINs with the editable macro .s.
!src/data/anim_085A0EA0/dat_anim_085A0EA0.s
# NON_MATCHING staging (D26): the readable C in src/nonmatching/*.c is tracked,
# but the agbcc .s intermediate from `make nonmatching` is a build artifact.
src/nonmatching/*.s

# Carve glue GENERATED from the layout/ manifests by scripts/gen_layout.py and
# regenerated at build time (Makefile). NOT committed, so parallel carves never
# conflict on them; each carve writes only its own per-task fragment under
# layout/<name>.d/. See docs/decisions.md.
/ldscript.txt
/asm/baserom.s
/asm/jp_syms.s

# src/msg_data.c is GENERATED-AND-COMMITTED from texts/jp_texts.txt by
# scripts/texttools/msg_jp.py build-c (re-Huffman-encodes the JP message block
# as compiled C, byte-identical after link). It is COMMITTED (the src/*.c wildcard
# must see it on a fresh checkout); only the agbcc intermediate src/msg_data.s is
# ignored (via src/*.s above). The higher-level source is texts/jp_*.txt. See
# docs/text.md.

# Per-task layout fragments (layout/<name>.d/*.tsv) ARE committed -- they are the
# parallel-carve mechanism. The generic `*.d` rule above (for make dependency
# files) otherwise hides these directories, so re-include them explicitly.
!/layout/carved_rom.d/
!/layout/carved_ram.d/
!/layout/baseline_syms.d/
!/layout/baseline_syms_drop.d/
!/layout/patches.d/
!/layout/carved_rom.d/*.tsv
!/layout/carved_ram.d/*.tsv
!/layout/baseline_syms.d/*.tsv
!/layout/baseline_syms_drop.d/*.tsv
!/layout/patches.d/*.tsv

# Locally-installed toolchain (install agbcc the same way as the US decomp)
/tools/agbcc

# decomp-permuter: upstream clone + its work dirs are local (set up via
# scripts/permuter/setup.sh). permuter_settings.toml + scripts/permuter/ are tracked.
/tools/decomp-permuter
/nonmatchings/
# Local decomp-permuter scratch: candidate <Fn>.c + target <Fn>.s pairs and *.wip
# experiments (see docs/frontier.md, docs/handoff.md). Never committed -- a matched
# result is ported into src/ + wired via layout/ fragments, not kept as scratch.
/_permwork/

# mizuchi: matching-decomp pipeline orchestrator (macabeus/mizuchi), vendored
# locally via scripts/tools/mizuchi/setup.sh. The setup script + FE8J config
# (scripts/tools/mizuchi/) and docs/tools/mizuchi.md are tracked.
/tools/mizuchi
# Root-level state mizuchi generates when run from the repo root (the config is
# copied/symlinked here, and outputDir/promptsDir resolve to the project root):
# the config copy, the codebase index, the prompt sets, and the run outputs.
# outputDir writes timestamped FILES (run-report-<ts>.html / run-results-<ts>.json
# and their partial-* variants) plus the claude-cache.json cache file — match the
# actual upstream filenames, not directories. All transient.
/mizuchi.yaml
/mizuchi-db.json
/prompts/
/run-report-*.html
/run-results-*.json
/partial-run-report-*.html
/partial-run-results-*.json
/claude-cache.json
# asm-differ: upstream clone is local (set up via scripts/tools/asm-differ/setup.sh).
# diff_settings.py (repo root) + docs/tools/asm-differ.md are tracked; the venv
# lives outside the repo (default $HOME/asm-differ-venv, like the permuter's).
/tools/asm-differ
# m2c (asm->C decompiler): upstream clone is local (set up via
# scripts/tools/m2c/setup.sh). The wrapper scripts under scripts/tools/m2c/
# and docs/tools/m2c.md are tracked.
/tools/m2c
# The m2c context file is GENERATED (scripts/tools/m2c/gen_ctx.py from
# include/global.h); the generator is committed, the large flattened ctx is not.
fe8j_ctx.c

# Claude Code: share settings.json + loop_prompt.md, but keep local/transient
# state out (per-user overrides and the ralph-loop session-state file).
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.md
.claude/*.local.json
# Agent-tool worktrees (isolation:worktree) are planted inside the repo —
# transient build dirs that must never be tracked or travel on branches.
.claude/worktrees/

# Parallel-carving local coordination state (scripts/parallel/claim.py): task
# claims + the registry lock. Local only — must NOT travel on per-task branches.
/layout/claims/

